---
title: "recordAttendance (AttendanceZen: Blueprint)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_normalize: normalizedCardId = cardId.replace(/:/, '').toLowerCase()
    q_normalize --> q_lookup: SELECT from attendance.users WHERE card_id = normalizedCardId
    q_lookup --> q_error_unregistered: attendanceUser not found
    q_error_unregistered --> [*]: return success=false, "unregistered card"
    q_lookup --> q_fetch_member: attendanceUser found, userId = supabase_auth_user_id
    q_fetch_member --> q_fetch_nickname: SELECT discord_uid FROM member.members WHERE supabase_auth_user_id = userId
    q_fetch_nickname --> q_resolve_name: discord_uid exists
    q_fetch_nickname --> q_default_name: discord_uid missing
    q_resolve_name --> q_check_last: displayName = fetchMemberNickname(discord_uid)
    q_default_name --> q_check_last: displayName = default
    q_check_last --> q_determine_type: SELECT last attendance WHERE user_id = userId AND date = today ORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT 1
    q_determine_type --> q_set_in: no previous record today
    q_determine_type --> q_set_out: lastType = 'in'
    q_determine_type --> q_set_in: lastType = 'out'
    q_set_in --> q_insert: attendanceType = 'in'
    q_set_out --> q_insert: attendanceType = 'out'
    q_insert --> q_error_insert: INSERT INTO attendance.attendances fails
    q_error_insert --> [*]: return success=false, "recording failed"
    q_insert --> q_success: INSERT succeeds
    q_success --> [*]: revalidatePath, return success=true, type, displayName

    note right of q_normalize
        INV-001: cardId is normalized (lowercase, no colons) before lookup
        INV-002: attendance type toggles based on last record for today
        INV-003: first scan of day always records 'in'
    end note
